In the early 1980s when I was a junior sysadmin,
the account "games" owned the /usr/games tree and
it's VMS equivalent.  BSD 4.2/3 on VAX and SunOS
3.x on 68K.

Over the years as games became less used on Unix
the account "games", the group "games" and
eventually the games section of the man pages
went away.  At one point games were training
tools for programming techniques.  My original
mentor in the SA field had written "rain" to
teach how to use the curses/termcap/termlib
library routines.

